## Deployment & DevOps Guardrails

### Forensic V2 live Edge Function deploy path

Approved live Forensic V2 Supabase project ref: `zgsofkgddpcntdvpckdq`.

Some stale docs may call this ref "staging"; operator intent treats it as the approved live Forensic V2 target.

For live/Forensic V2 Edge Function deployment, the only approved path is the human-operated wrapper:

```powershell
$env:SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF = "zgsofkgddpcntdvpckdq"
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\deploy-functions-forensic-v2-live.ps1
```

That wrapper is currently scoped to deploy only:

- `start-upload-scan-session`
- `capture-truth-gate-lead`

### AI agent prohibitions

Cursor/AI agents must not run raw Supabase deployment or mutation commands.

Agents must not run, and must not recommend that the agent run:

- `supabase functions deploy`
- `npx supabase functions deploy`
- `supabase db push`
- `npx supabase db push`
- `supabase db reset`
- `npx supabase db reset`
- `supabase secrets set`
- `npx supabase secrets set`
- `supabase gen types`
- `npx supabase gen types`
- `npm run typegen`
- any Supabase deploy command using `--prune`

Agents must not execute the wrapper themselves:

- `.\scripts\deploy-functions-forensic-v2-live.ps1`
- `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\deploy-functions-forensic-v2-live.ps1`

The wrapper is human-operator only.

When a deployment is requested, stop before execution and instruct the human operator to run the wrapper locally from a clean working tree on branch `forensic_report_v2` with:

- `SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=zgsofkgddpcntdvpckdq`
- confirmation phrase `DEPLOY_FORENSIC_V2_LIVE_FUNCTIONS`

### Forbidden target refs

For Forensic V2 work, never target:

- `wkrcyxcnzhwjtdpmfpaf` — legacy Lovable/main production
- `wm-mvp-forensic-v2-local` — local Docker namespace in `supabase/config.toml`
- blank or unset project refs
- any ref other than `zgsofkgddpcntdvpckdq` for live/Forensic V2 Edge Function deploys

Do not treat `supabase/config.toml` `project_id` or `supabase/.temp/project-ref` as proof of a safe deploy target. The wrapper's explicit `--project-ref` is authoritative.

### Source edits and deploys stay separate

When editing Edge Function source, separate code changes from deployment.

After source edits, explain verification steps and tell the human operator to run the secured wrapper if deployment is approved. Do not combine opaque "edit + deploy" actions in one agent pass.

